Below is a quick “data‑map” of the columns that appear most useful for building the ERCOT 2022‑10‑01 Daily Market Dynamics report, followed by 10 exploratory Snowflake SQL statements (from very simple to a bit more complex) that you can run to understand the data before constructing the final report.  
All identifiers (`DATABASE.SCHEMA.TABLE` and column names) are quoted exactly as they appear in the catalog.

────────────────────────────────────────
Key columns and their potential usage
────────────────────────────────────────
1. ISO_MARKET_TIMES_SAMPLE  
   • "ISO": filter to 'ERCOT'  
   • "DATETIME", "MARKETDAY": link to hourly rows & day bucket  
   • "ONPEAK", "OFFPEAK", "WEPEAK", "WDPEAK": peak/off‑peak flags  
   • "TIMEZONE": local zone for the date

2. DART_PRICES_SAMPLE (hourly DA/RT prices)  
   • "OBJECTID": 10000697078 (HB_NORTH)  
   • "DATETIME": hour ending timestamp  
   • "DALMP", "RTLMP": day‑ahead / real‑time LMP values  
   • "RTFINAL": use ‘Y’ rows only  
   • "TIMEZONE": align with ISO_MARKET_TIMES_SAMPLE

3. RT15_PRICES_SAMPLE (15‑min real‑time prices)  
   • Same "OBJECTID" and "DATETIME" to derive hourly average if desired  
   • "LMP": finer‑granularity real‑time price

4. TS_FORECAST_SAMPLE (all forecast series)  
   • "DATATYPEID":  
        – 19060  → Load forecast  
        – 9285   → Wind gen forecast  
        – 662    → Solar gen forecast  
   • "OBJECTID": 10000712973 (North Load Zone)  
   • "DATETIME": forecasted hour  
   • "VALUE": forecasted MW  
   • "PUBLISHDATE": vintage (keep latest for 2022‑10‑01 if needed)  
   • "TIMEZONE": local zone

5. TS_LOAD_SAMPLE (hourly actual load)  
   • "OBJECTID": 10000712973  
   • "DATETIME": hour ending  
   • "VALUE": actual load (MW)

6. RT_LOADS_SAMPLE (sub‑hour real‑time loads)  
   • Can be aggregated to hourly if higher resolution desired

7. TS_GEN_SAMPLE (actual generation)  
   • "DATATYPEID":  
        – 16  → Wind gen actual  
        – 650 → Solar gen actual  
   • "OBJECTID": 10000712973 (confirm availability)

8. DS_OBJECT_LIST_SAMPLE & PRICE_NODES_SAMPLE  
   • Map "OBJECTID" ↔ names / zones for sanity checks

────────────────────────────────────────
Typical filters / join keys
────────────────────────────────────────
• Date window: `"DATETIME" >= '2022-10-01 00:00:00' AND "DATETIME" < '2022-10-02 00:00:00'`  
• Node price: `"OBJECTID" = 10000697078`  
• Load zone & generation: `"OBJECTID" = 10000712973`  
• Forecast series: match the appropriate `"DATATYPEID"`  
• Peak tags: join on `"DATETIME"` (hourly) between data tables and ISO_MARKET_TIMES_SAMPLE  
• Keep `"RTFINAL" = 'Y'` where applicable

────────────────────────────────────────
10 sample Snowflake SQL queries
────────────────────────────────────────
```sql
-- 1) Description: Quick look at the ERCOT market‑day and peak/off‑peak flags for 2022‑10‑01.
SELECT "ISO",
       "DATETIME",
       "ONPEAK",
       "OFFPEAK",
       "WEPEAK",
       "WDPEAK",
       "MARKETDAY"
FROM   "YES_ENERGY__SAMPLE_DATA"."YES_ENERGY_SAMPLE"."ISO_MARKET_TIMES_SAMPLE"
WHERE  "ISO" = 'ERCOT'
  AND  "MARKETDAY" = '2022-10-01 00:00:00'
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Description: Hourly Day‑Ahead (DALMP) and Real‑Time (RTLMP) prices at price node 10000697078 on 1‑Oct‑2022.
SELECT "DATETIME",
       "TIMEZONE",
       "DALMP",
       "RTLMP"
FROM   "YES_ENERGY__SAMPLE_DATA"."YES_ENERGY_SAMPLE"."DART_PRICES_SAMPLE"
WHERE  "OBJECTID" = 10000697078
  AND  "RTFINAL" = 'Y'
  AND  "DATETIME" >= '2022-10-01 00:00:00'
  AND  "DATETIME" <  '2022-10-02 00:00:00'
ORDER BY "DATETIME"
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Description: 15‑minute real‑time LMP values to inspect volatility on 1‑Oct‑2022.
SELECT "DATETIME",
       "LMP"
FROM   "YES_ENERGY__SAMPLE_DATA"."YES_ENERGY_SAMPLE"."RT15_PRICES_SAMPLE"
WHERE  "OBJECTID" = 10000697078
  AND  "DATETIME" >= '2022-10-01 00:00:00'
  AND  "DATETIME" <  '2022-10-02 00:00:00'
ORDER BY "DATETIME"
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Description: Distinct forecast datatype IDs available for object 10000712973 (help confirm 19060, 9285, 662 exist).
SELECT DISTINCT "DATATYPEID"
FROM   "YES_ENERGY__SAMPLE_DATA"."YES_ENERGY_SAMPLE"."TS_FORECAST_SAMPLE"
WHERE  "OBJECTID" = 10000712973
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Description: Hourly load forecast (datatypeid 19060) for North zone on 1‑Oct‑2022 (latest publishes kept).
SELECT "DATETIME",
       "VALUE" AS "LOAD_FORECAST_MW",
       "PUBLISHDATE"
FROM   "YES_ENERGY__SAMPLE_DATA"."YES_ENERGY_SAMPLE"."TS_FORECAST_SAMPLE"
WHERE  "OBJECTID"   = 10000712973
  AND  "DATATYPEID" = 19060
  AND  "DATETIME"  >= '2022-10-01 00:00:00'
  AND  "DATETIME"  <  '2022-10-02 00:00:00'
ORDER BY "DATETIME", "PUBLISHDATE" DESC
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Description: Actual hourly load (MW) for 1‑Oct‑2022 from TS_LOAD_SAMPLE (datatypeid 9641 shown in sample).
SELECT "DATETIME",
       "VALUE" AS "ACTUAL_LOAD_MW"
FROM   "YES_ENERGY__SAMPLE_DATA"."YES_ENERGY_SAMPLE"."TS_LOAD_SAMPLE"
WHERE  "OBJECTID" = 10000712973
  AND  "DATETIME" >= '2022-10-01 00:00:00'
  AND  "DATETIME" <  '2022-10-02 00:00:00'
ORDER BY "DATETIME"
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Description: Wind generation forecast (datatypeid 9285) for 1‑Oct‑2022.
SELECT "DATETIME",
       "VALUE" AS "WIND_GEN_FORECAST_MW",
       "PUBLISHDATE"
FROM   "YES_ENERGY__SAMPLE_DATA"."YES_ENERGY_SAMPLE"."TS_FORECAST_SAMPLE"
WHERE  "OBJECTID"   = 10000712973
  AND  "DATATYPEID" = 9285
  AND  "DATETIME"  >= '2022-10-01 00:00:00'
  AND  "DATETIME"  <  '2022-10-02 00:00:00'
ORDER BY "DATETIME"
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 8) Description: Wind generation actuals (datatypeid 16) on 1‑Oct‑2022.  Check if North zone object exists.
SELECT "DATETIME",
       "VALUE" AS "WIND_GEN_ACTUAL_MW"
FROM   "YES_ENERGY__SAMPLE_DATA"."YES_ENERGY_SAMPLE"."TS_GEN_SAMPLE"
WHERE  "OBJECTID"   = 10000712973   -- adjust if not populated for this object
  AND  "DATATYPEID" = 16
  AND  "DATETIME"  >= '2022-10-01 00:00:00'
  AND  "DATETIME"  <  '2022-10-02 00:00:00'
ORDER BY "DATETIME"
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 9) Description: Solar generation forecast (datatypeid 662) on 1‑Oct‑2022.
SELECT "DATETIME",
       "VALUE" AS "SOLAR_GEN_FORECAST_MW",
       "PUBLISHDATE"
FROM   "YES_ENERGY__SAMPLE_DATA"."YES_ENERGY_SAMPLE"."TS_FORECAST_SAMPLE"
WHERE  "OBJECTID"   = 10000712973
  AND  "DATATYPEID" = 662
  AND  "DATETIME"  >= '2022-10-01 00:00:00'
  AND  "DATETIME"  <  '2022-10-02 00:00:00'
ORDER BY "DATETIME"
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 10) Description: Solar generation actuals (datatypeid 650) on 1‑Oct‑2022.
SELECT "DATETIME",
       "VALUE" AS "SOLAR_GEN_ACTUAL_MW"
FROM   "YES_ENERGY__SAMPLE_DATA"."YES_ENERGY_SAMPLE"."TS_GEN_SAMPLE"
WHERE  "OBJECTID"   = 10000712973   -- adjust if necessary
  AND  "DATATYPEID" = 650
  AND  "DATETIME"  >= '2022-10-01 00:00:00'
  AND  "DATETIME"  <  '2022-10-02 00:00:00'
ORDER BY "DATETIME"
LIMIT  20;
```

These queries should confirm the availability of each data slice, its time zone, and any idiosyncrasies (e.g., whether wind/solar actuals are stored on the same `"OBJECTID"`).  
Once verified, you can join the hourly datasets on `"DATETIME"` and compute:

• net_load_forecast = load_forecast − wind_gen_forecast − solar_gen_forecast  
• net_load_real_time = actual_load − wind_gen_actual − solar_gen_actual

together with the peak/off‑peak flags from ISO_MARKET_TIMES_SAMPLE to complete the final operations & efficiency report for 2022‑10‑01.
